# BookmarkForge — 6 exact alerts — production cron
# Copia este archivo a /etc/cron.d/bookmarkforge o usa `crontab -e`
#
# Requires: PROD_BASE_URL and SLACK_WEBHOOK (optional) in the environment
# The checks already live in the code: storageMonitor + productionMonitor + bundleIntegrity
# + clientEventReporter + retry-stats + degradation probing

# ALERTA 1: APP CAÍDA — cada 60s verifica nginx + api + WS + CSP
# Every isolated failure → Slack alert. With APP_DOWN_AUTO_ROLLBACK=1, TWO
# CONSECUTIVE failures (counter persisted across cron ticks) trigger automatic
# rollback and then rollback.mjs --verify confirms recovery BEFORE notifying:
# verify OK → NO operator alert (the rollback resolved it); verify FAIL →
# escalate. Rollback/recovery verified with mocks (see scripts/__tests__).
# Automatic rollback enabled (fail-closed: without this var NO rollback runs):
#   APP_DOWN_AUTO_ROLLBACK=1
# Consecutive-failure threshold (default 2):
#   APP_DOWN_THRESHOLD=2
# Comandos de rollback/verify (default node scripts/rollback.mjs --auto / --verify):
#   ROLLBACK_CMD='node scripts/rollback.mjs --auto'
#   ROLLBACK_VERIFY_CMD='node scripts/rollback.mjs --verify'
* * * * * PROD_BASE_URL=https://tu-dominio.com SLACK_WEBHOOK=https://hooks.slack.com/services/T.../B.../... APP_DOWN_AUTO_ROLLBACK=1 /usr/bin/node /app/scripts/monitoring-alerts.mjs >> /var/log/bmf-monitoring.log 2>&1 || echo "ALERTA APP_CAIDA $(date)" | tee -a /var/log/bmf-monitoring.log

# ALERT 1 (simple alternative without Slack): log and exit code only
# * * * * * PROD_BASE_URL=https://tu-dominio.com /usr/bin/node /app/scripts/production-smoke.mjs >> /var/log/bmf-smoke.log 2>&1 || /usr/local/bin/bmf-page.sh

# ALERTA 2: BUNDLE CORRUPTO — se detecta en cliente via bundleIntegrity.ts:recordIntegritySpike
# Each `bundle-integrity-failed` increments a counter. 3 failures within 5min fire the `bundle-integrity-spike` event
# The server can count CSP violations via /csp-report:
# En nginx log: tail -F /var/log/nginx/access.log | grep csp-report | awk '{print $1}' | sort | uniq -c
# If >10/min → alert. Already in productionMonitor.ts:recordCspViolation (threshold 10)

# ALERTA 3: STORAGE PRESSURE + BUNDLE INTEGRITY — cliente cada 5min via storageMonitor.ts
# Si pct>80% → evento `storage-pressure` (pressure). Si >90% → critical.
# The client already shows a QuotaExceededError toast (src/main.tsx:172).
# IMPLEMENTED: the client forwards storage-pressure / bundle-integrity-spike /
# error-spike to POST /api/client-events (same-origin, gated by bmf_local_error_storage).
# error-spike: 3 errores globales (window error / unhandledrejection) en 60s →
# evento window `error-spike` en productionMonitor.ts (recordGlobalError).
# The server alerts when >= 3 clients report critical within 10 min:
#   - Log estructurado `client_events_critical_threshold` (la alerta primaria)
#   - Webhook opcional: CLIENT_EVENTS_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/...
# Tunables: CLIENT_EVENTS_CRITICAL_CLIENTS (default 3), CLIENT_EVENTS_WINDOW_MS (default 600000)
# Diagnostics (requires a token):
#   curl -H 'x-client-events-admin-token: <CLIENT_EVENTS_ADMIN_TOKEN>' https://tu-dominio.com/api/client-events

# ALERT 4: CLIENT_CRITICAL — cluster of critical clients → PAGE + AUTO ROLLBACK
# monitoring-alerts.mjs reads the server log (client_events_critical_threshold
# with timestamp) and escalates: page (PAGE_CMD) + automatic rollback (AUTO_ROLLBACK=1).
# In production with docker logs the default already works; for file logs:
#   CLIENT_EVENTS_LOG_FILE=/var/log/bmf-server.log
# Automatic rollback enabled (fail-closed: without this var NO rollback runs):
#   AUTO_ROLLBACK=1
# Optional page command (e.g. SMS/PagerDuty script):
#   PAGE_CMD=/usr/local/bin/bmf-page.sh
# Anti-loop cooldown between page/rollback (default 600000 ms):
#   ROLLBACK_COOLDOWN_MS=600000

# ALERT 5: RETRY_DEGRADED — clients that lost events after bounded retries
# The reporter POSTs counters to /api/client-events/retry-stats; the server logs
# `client_events_retry_degraded` on new drops. monitoring-alerts consumes the
# same log source (CLIENT_EVENTS_LOG_FILE / CLIENT_EVENTS_LOG_CMD) and PAGES
# (PAGE_CMD, cooldown). Never rollback: this is delivery health, not a code regression.

# ALERT 6: API_DEGRADED — degradation (not an outage): /health p95 + error-rate
# Probes /health N times per tick and fails when p95 > threshold or error-rate > threshold.
# Page (PAGE_CMD, cooldown); NEVER rollback (total outage = APP_DOWN).
# Thresholds (defaults):
#   API_PROBE_SAMPLES=10        /health samples per tick
#   API_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=5000   timeout per sample (ms)
#   API_LATENCY_P95_MS=1000     p95 >= 1000 ms = degraded
#   API_ERROR_RATE=0.2          >= 20% failed samples = degraded

# VERIFICACIÓN MANUAL:
# node scripts/monitoring-alerts.mjs --json
# node scripts/prod-blindeo-checklist.mjs
# node scripts/rollback.mjs --list
# npm run check:blindeo
